    <dashboard enable-sort-zone-taborder='true' name='UK Retail II — Chapter Four: Self-Service Drill-Down Dashboard'>
      <style />
      <size maxheight='800' maxwidth='1000' minheight='800' minwidth='1000' />
      <zones>
        <zone h='47125' id='3' name='Funnel Tier Overview' w='44900' x='300' y='1000' />
        <zone h='51625' id='13' name='Frequency Spike Overview' w='44800' x='500' y='47875' />
        <zone forceUpdate='true' h='23500' id='18' type-v2='text' w='43500' x='45100' y='13375'>
          <formatted-text>
            <run fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Tableau Regular' fontsize='12' italic='true'>Funnel Tier Overview</run>
            <run fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Tableau Regular' fontsize='12'>: </run>
            <run>Æ&#10;</run>
            <run fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Benton Sans Book' fontsize='12'>Customers split by recency and net spend. Lapsed Whale requires recency &gt; 377 days and net spend ≥ £2,180.28 — a small population (58) that breaks the otherwise steady decline in spend as recency increases. Never Converted (23) and Lapsed Whale (58) are visually near-flat at this scale but represent real populations, not missing data.</run>
          </formatted-text>
        </zone>
        <zone h='18375' id='19' type-v2='text' w='45200' x='45700' y='66125'>
          <formatted-text>
            <run fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Tableau Regular' fontsize='11' italic='true'>Frequency Spike Overview:</run>
            <run fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Tableau Regular' fontsize='11'>Æ </run>
            <run>Æ&#10;</run>
            <run fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Tableau Regular' fontsize='11'>Top Decile (Spike Zone) = net spend ≥ £5,224.45 (90th percentile). Order frequency spikes sharply at this threshold rather than gradually across the top 15–20%, as Chapter Three&apos;s initial chart-rotation estimate suggested.</run>
            <run>Æ&#10;</run>
          </formatted-text>
        </zone>
      </zones>
